Something occured to me the other day: there are dozens and dozens of weapon
types in the game which I never use.

I use whatever my character starts out with, plus:
- daggers (wielded and thrown)
- darts (if I don't have enough daggers, or if I can poison them)
- bow and arrow (rarely, unless a ranger)
- long sword
- silver saber
- unicorn horn (against rust monsters & friends)

If I find any of these, I stick with what I have, even if that is just
daggers or a short sword:
- knives
- axes
- two-handed swords
- blunt weapons
- polearms and spears
- crossbows
- throwing stars

I find that they aren't worth the trouble, especially when you have to work
your weapon skills in a direction which will be useful later in the game.

Crossbow arrows and throwing stars are too rare for me to bother with them.

My question is: does everyone use the same weapon strategy as I do?

And do any of you run around in mid- or deep-level games with anything but
artifact swords, the other major artifact weapons, and heavily enchanted
silver sabers?  Does anyone bother making crysknives these days?

